//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// House - First Impressions Dialogue

title: ApproachingHouse
---
<<play_emote player_emote drop>>

Dawn: No wonder Grams never told me about this place.
Dawn: It’s gonna be a fixer upper.
===



//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Spirit 1st Dialogue

title: FirstSpiritIntro
---
// Variables ---------------------------------------------
<<declare $spiritExplained = false>>

// Dialogue Jumper ---------------------------------------
<<declare $spiritTalkTo = 0>>

<<if $spiritTalkTo == 1>>
    <<jump SpiritFiller1>>
<<elseif $spiritTalkTo == 2>>
    <<jump finishedIntroMinigame>>
<<endif>>
//---------------------------------------


<<set $spiritTalkTo = 1>>
<<play_cutscene PlayerCutsceneAnimator character_scared>>
<<play_cutscene CutsceneAnimator spirit-appear>>
<<play_emote_plain player_emote exclaim>>
Dawn: It that a… <shake>ghost?!</shake>
Dawn: Nup, nope, I’m out of here. Sorry Grams. <sketchy><b>This is just too much.<sketchy></b>.

Spirit: <shake>Wait, wait!</shake>
Spirit: Wow, it’s been a long time since I’ve seen a human here.
Spirit: Are you… wait, <b>I know you</b>. Or, at least, I think I do…
Spirit: <b>Anne</b>, is that you? You’ve gotten younger. And leaner.

Dawn: That’s my Grandma you’re talking about. My name's Dawn.

Spirit: Grandma? I didn’t think it had been <b>that</b> long.
Spirit: It’s nice to meet you, Dawn.
    -> It's nice to meet you too!
        <<play_cutscene PlayerCutsceneAnimator character_wave>>
        Dawn: Well it's a pleasure to meet you too... ghost?
        Spirit: Well, I'm spirit. Technically. But...
        <<set $spiritExplained to true>>
    -> What are you doing here?
        <<play_cutscene PlayerCutsceneAnimator character_scared>>
        Dawn: What are you doing in my Grandma's house?
        Spirit: I live here.
Spirit: She. This place. It’s been left alone so long, that all my friends have left. Now, it’s just me. 
Spirit: I don’t get why she would just leave us. This place broke down, and the spiritual energy with it.
Spirit: But, now you’re here, maybe you can help!

//Go through backstory and then come back
->So, you're a ghost...?
    <<detour spiritBackstory>>
->Okay, why are you <b>here</b>?
    <<detour spiritLocationBackstory>>
->Help, how?
    <<detour spiritHelp>>
//

Dawn: I don’t mean to sound rude, but do you have to live here? 
Dawn: I'm not so sure about a little spirit hovering around me while I'm trying to get my bearings.

Spirit: I suppose that's fair. But, spirits need these spaces. They remind us of who we are, and they help us connect with humans so we don’t become <b>lost</b>. 
Spirit: And you don't want to see a lost spirit, they are quite… <wave>haunting</wave>.
Spirit: <i>Brrrr.</i> Anyways, we can make this a pleasant exchange! What were you planning on doing here?

Dawn: I’ve been thinking I want to work in a cafe. I like cooking and making coffee. Plus, I would like to meet some new people.

Spirit: Hm, then why don't we set up <b>Anne's Cafe</b> again?

Dawn: Anne had a cafe? <i>That must have been the second building mentioned in the will</i>...

Spirit: Yes! That's how Anne kept the people and spirits <b>happy</b>! 
Spirit: And when more spirits come back, <b>they can teach you some new recipes</b> too! You see, we nature spirits kinda have a <wave>knack</wave> for these things.

Dawn: Wait, there’s gonna be <b>more</b> of you?

Spirit: Don’t worry, they’re nice! <i>Well, most</i>. 
Spirit: When we start <b>cleaning up</b> and <b>helping more people</b> here, more of us will come home!

// Lead in to minigame
Dawn: Great.

Spirit: Now, let’s get to cooking! Your Grandma left a recipe book around here. I’ll grab it for you. 
Spirit: *The spirit whizzes around the room and conjures up a dusty recipe book.*
Spirit: Hmmm, let's see here. How about you show us your skills by whipping me up a delicious plate of <grow>Waffles</grow>?

Dawn: You're kidding me right?

Spirit: Haha. No. 
Spirit: Grab that apron and the ingredients. I'll wait here for you.
===
//
// 1st Dialogue Branch -------------------------------------------------------
//
title: spiritBackstory
---
    Dawn: So, you're a ghost haunting my grandma's House?

    <<if $spiritExplained == true>>
        Spirit: We've been over this already.
    <<endif>>

    Spirit: I’m not a ghost. More a <wave>“spirit of nature”</wave>.
    Spirit: And in regards to haunting; I'm far too <swing>cute</swing> to participate in such <sketchy>dubious</sketchy> activities.
    Spirit: Though, 

    Dawn: A "spirit of nature"? What's that?

    Spirit: We are mediators between people and nature! Well, used to be...
    Spirit: Long ago, this town was a place of strong spiritual energy. The people worked together and made this place strong.
    Spirit: But, when Anne left, people forgot about us and they started having their own troubles... 
    Spirit: Because of that, many spirits started to move on.

    
===
//
//
title: spiritLocationBackstory
---
    Dawn: What are you doing in Grams' house?

    Spirit: Well, I live here! Long ago, the people of this town all worked together and got along, and this town became one of strong spiritual energy. 
    Spirit: We lived happily and Anne took care of us.
    Spirit: But, this place is long past its glory days, and that’s why the spirits who lived here left. 
    Spirit: More mould and mildew, less <wave>spiritual buzz</wave>, y’know.
===
//
//
title: spiritHelp
---
    Dawn: You want my help? Why?

    Spirit: Long ago, this town was a place of strong spiritual energy. The people worked together and made this place strong.
    Spirit: We lived happily and Anne took care of us.
    Spirit: But, when Anne left, people forgot about us and they started having their own troubles... 
    Spirit: Because of that, many spirits started to move on.
===



//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Filler Dialogue - After 1st Dialogue

title:SpiritFiller1
---
Spirit: Once you've gotten those ingredients, you can get to cooking!
===



//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Spirit Tranformation Dialogue

title: finishedIntroMinigame
---
Spirit: Oh my! That looks <wave>delicious</wave>!

Dawn: See? Easy as pie.

Spirit: More like, waffles. Mmmm! It tastes amazing!
Spirit: Actually, I'm feeling inspired. 
Spirit: Hold up, I'm feeling <shake><b>really</b></shake> inspired.

Dawn: Are you... okay?

<<play_cutscene CutsceneAnimator seapancake-appear>>

Spirit: Well, well, well. I forgot I could do this. 

Dawn: Turn into food?

Spirit: It only happens when we're feeling more in touch. All nature spirits can turn into embodiments of nature, processed or not. 
Spirit: It helps us relate to you better.

Dawn: So people don't get scared of floating balls of light?

Spirit: Exactly!
Spirit: Let's not wait, I'll meet you at the cafe! It's just down the road.
Spirit: I'm sure the people here will be <sketchy><b>estatic</b></sketchy> to have something new here!

<<view_model ModelViewerUI waffle>>
===



//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Spirit "Breakfast Toast" Cooking Dialogue

title: tutorialMainMinigame
---
Spirit: Dawn, its time to cook!
Spirit: But first you need to prep those tomatoes.
Spirit: Use <sprite=1> to cut the tomatoes.
===

title: CompletedCutting
---
Spirit: Good job!
Spirit: Now use [m1/] to drag the tomato cuts onto the tray.
Spirit: Then we can begin the cooking process!
===

title: CookingBacon
---
Spirit: Nice work!
Spirit: Before cooking you must drag the olive oil onto the grill.
Spirit: <sprite=1> to pour the oil onto the grill.
Spirit: Be sure to keep topping up the oil.
Spirit: Use [m1/] to drag the food onto the grill.
Spirit: When the food is cooked use <sprite=1> to flip the food.
Spirit: After the food is cooked, place it onto the tray.
===

title: Plating
---
Spirit: Nice!
Spirit: Now place all the food onto the tray!
Spirit: Then ring the bell to finish.
===

















